    "title": "LDS Church announces change to weekly meeting schedules",
    "text": "NewsLocal News Actions Facebook Tweet Email LDS Church announces change to weekly schedules with Sunday School and other meetings Prev Next By: Spencer Burt Posted 9:09 PM, Mar 30, 2026 and last updated 12:13 AM, Mar 31, 2026 SALT LAKE CITY — For the second time in under eight years, The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints is significantly changing the way Sunday meetings will take place. In October 2018, LDS Church leaders announced that the total service would run for two hours instead of three. This meant alternating Sunday School and Priesthood/Relief Society/Young Women each week. The change became effective in January 2019. 1/1 Skip Ad Continue watchingafter the adVisit Advertiser websiteGO TO PAGEOn Monday, the church announced that starting Sept. 6, local wards will hold both Sunday School and the above-mentioned meetings every week, but for just 25 minutes each. Sacrament Meetings will continue to be one hour long. After the 2018 change, there was a 10-minute transition time between Sacrament Meeting and individual classes. There will now be a 5-minute break between the three different meetings. Primary and nursery, which are for children under the age of 12, will now be 55 minutes long instead of 50. Recent Local Utah Stories Weber 911 celebrates dispatchers during NPSTW Mythili Gubbi 13 minutes ago Weber 911 celebrates dispatchers during National Public Safety Telecommunicators Week 23 minutes ago Utah students celebrate Live Nation ruled an illegal monopoly Scott McKane 50 minutes ago 'It’s time to break it up' Utah students celebrate Live Nation ruled an illegal monopoly 1 hour and 4 minutes ago Recommended For You Marketplace Sell Your Items - Free to List Visit Full Marketplace University of Texas Football Shirts, Longhorns Football swea... $20 SportServer P. | sellwild.com Ohio State OSU Buckeyes White Spaghetti Tank $36 SportServer P. | sellwild.com Gridiron Heritage Two Tone Limited Snapback Hat $30 SportServer P. | sellwild.co